<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $186.1 mln June 24.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $186.1 mln June 24.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $186.1 million surplus on June 24 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown:</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JUNE 24</p>
<p>Exports: $193.9 million</p>
<p>Imports: $284.1 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $819.9 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $543.6 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $186.1 million</p>
<p>JUNE DOLLAR FLOWS TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.744 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $4.534 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $6.856 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $6.106 billion</p>
<p>Net deficit: $39.6 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
